  "homeHelp": "Your home is a node that stays on power in one place. It keeps texts to you while your phone is away, and your card carries its address, so the card stays good wherever you go. The inbox button on the first screen, Fetch my mail, brings them to the node you are on.\n\nWithout a home your card is temporary: it names the node you use now, which keeps your mail only while you come back to it.\n\nTo make a node your home, the phone pairs with it. A friend who owns a home node can also give you a home there from afar.\n\nWhen you choose another home, or none, your old home sends you the mail it keeps, then forgets you.\n\nA home that stops answering may be off or out of reach, or may have lost your place there. Fetch again later; if it still does not answer, make another node your home, or choose Remove home.\n\nUse my existing home is for a phone that got your identity back from your 12 words: give your home's address, and once your home answers it is your home again.",
  "@homeHelp": {
    "description": "The help on the home node. Fetch my mail, Remove home and Use my existing home are the buttons commonFetch, homeRemove and homeUseExisting."
  },
  "homePeopleHelp": "As the owner you choose who has a home here, from anywhere: give a contact a home here from their conversation's menu, remove a person's home, or make someone else the owner.\n\nEach goes to your home with a fetch of your mail, and its answer comes back with it.",
